  "details": "I have confirmed information that we are preparing to migrate to 2021 (or 2022) LTS. 2022LTS will officially support \"Unity Physics\" by Unity. Could you please support this if possible?\n\n- Why?\n\nUnity Physics\" is faster and easier to deploy than \"PhysX\", Unity's built-in physics engine (just install the package and add \"Convert To Entit\" components!) ).\n\nThis engine supports Box, Capsule, Sphere, Cylinder, Plane, Convex, and Mesh colliders as well as the built-in one.\n\nIn the VRChat world, there are playthings such as \"chairs\" and \"balls\", most of which are controlled by \"Rigidbody\". A few of them are fine, but installing a large number of them will have a significant impact on performance. This is especially true for game worlds.\n\nComparing 6000 box objects, \"PhysX\" is stable at 15 FPS and \"Unity Physics\" is stable at 30-35 FPS.\n\nUnity Physics\" was in preview stage as of 2019.3.0f1, but moved to the official version at 2022LTS. It is a good time to introduce it.\n\nImplementing these features may require a major overhaul of the SDK, so it would be nice if you could just think about whether to include it in the roadmap or not.",
